[2026-11-27T07:01:56.427Z] [STDOUT] {"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_139","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '275,990p' dev/log/issues/20/pulls/21/CI-CD-BEST-PRACTICES.md | rg -n '\"'^#|CodeQL|lockfile|license|private|credentials|directory'\"' | head -110; sed -n '1,120p' scripts/check-file-size.mjs; git ls-tree -r --name-only origin/main; gh run view 45955618974 --json status,conclusion,jobs --jq '{status,conclusion,jobs:[.jobs[]|{name,conclusion}]}'\"","aggregated_output":"1:### 7. Validate the Actual Merge Result\n25:### 8. Pre-commit Hooks\n37:### 9. Release Automation\n45:- **Commit the version bump directly to the default branch** - The release job pushes its generated version commit (package metadata, lockfile, changelog, consumed changesets) straight to `main` as `github-actions[bot]`, and fails closed if that commit changes anything other than release metadata. Do not route it through an auto-merged release pull request: every release then adds one more pull request and one more branch (a no-deletion ruleset keeps it forever), and a failed run leaves an open release pull request behind for someone to close\n60:### 10. Concurrency Control\n123:#### Preserve a full check when a commit arrives\n135:### 11. Secrets Detection\n143:### 12. Documentation Validation\n159:### 13. Container Images: Native Runners per Architecture\n195:### 14. Lint the Workflows Themselves\n215:### 15. Audit the Dependency Tree\n217:**Code scanning does not audit your dependencies, and PR-scoped dependency review does not audit the ones you already have.** These two jobs look like coverage together and leave a hole between them: CodeQL analyses your source, while `dependency-review-action` runs only on `pull_request` and only inspects the dependencies a PR _changes_. An advisory published against a package that has been pinned for a year is invisible to both, forever, because no PR touches that line.\n223:- **Audit the lockfile as committed** (`--package-lock-only`). It reports what a consumer would get, and cannot be turned green by a resolution that only happens on this runner.\n227:### 16. Prove You Can Publish Before You Build\n243:      run: node scripts/preflight-credentials.mjs --mode \"$PREFLIGHT_MODE\"\n251:- **Report every failure, not the first.** The preflight's value is one report naming all missing credentials. A login step that aborts the job hides the rest, so make it `continue-on-error: true` and let the preflight script decide.\n252:- **Check reachability, not just writability.** A GHCR package is private on first push and stays private until someone clicks; publishing more versions of a package nobody can pull is exactly the compute this job exists to skip. GitHub exposes no API for package visibility (the packages REST API is GET/DELETE/restore only), so this is a manual step that the pipeline can only detect and name.\n254:- **Verify the published result anonymously, and separately.** Never gate the release on the push (a failed mirror must not delete a good release), but do check afterwards, with no credentials, that what you published can be pulled. A check that authenticates measures the publisher's view; a reader gets neither the login nor the benefit of the doubt.\n258:### 17. Tell a Broken Pipeline from a Changed World\n285:## Quality Enforcement Strategy\n305:## Getting Started\n314:### Add Swift CI to a multi-language repository\n317:2. Add a caller such as `.github/workflows/swift-checks.yml`. Give it `contents: read` and call `./.github/workflows/swift-ci.yml` with `mode: embedded` and `pipeline-directory: swift/ci`. Adapt the caller's triggers to your default branch and merge queue. [Swift monorepo guide and example caller](https://github.com/link-foundation/swift-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template/blob/main/docs/monorepo.md)\n318:3. Set `package-directory` to the directory containing `Package.swift` (`'.'` for a root manifest). Set `source-paths` to explicit repository-relative paths, one per line, for the manifest, `Package.resolved` if present, sources, tests and shared fixtures.\n321:## Automatic CI/CD Remediation\n337:### Why the issue is a Bug, and what it leaves out\n345:### Language → Template Mapping\n379:## References\n#!/usr/bin/env bun\n\nimport { execFileSync } from 'node:child_process';\nimport { readFileSync } from 'node:fs';\n\nconst MAX_LINES = 1100;\nconst files = new Set(\n  execFileSync(\n    'git',\n    [\n      'ls-files',\n      '-z',\n      '--cached',\n      '--others',\n      '--exclude-standard',\n      '--',\n      '*.js',\n      '*.mjs',\n      '*.cjs',\n    ],\n    { encoding: 'utf8' }\n  )\n    .split('\\0')\n    .filter(Boolean)\n);\nconst missing = new Set(\n  execFileSync('git', ['ls-files', '-z', '--deleted'], {\n    encoding: 'utf8',\n  }).split('\\0')\n);\n\nfor (const file of files) {\n  if (missing.has(file)) {\n    continue;\n  }\n  const text = readFileSync(file, 'utf8');\n  const lines = text\n    ? text.split('\\n').length - Number(text.endsWith('\\n'))\n    : 0;\n  if (lines > MAX_LINES) {\n    console.error(\n      `${file} exceeds the ${MAX_LINES}-line limit (${lines} lines).`\n    );\n    process.exitCode = 1;\n  }\n}\nif (!process.exitCode) {\n  console.log(`JavaScript files are within the ${MAX_LINES}-line limit.`);\n}\n.changeset/README.md\n.changeset/config.json\n.github/workflows/release.yml\n.gitignore\n.husky/pre-commit\n.jscpd.json\n.prettierignore\n.prettierrc\nCHANGELOG.md\nLICENSE\nREADME.md\nREQUIREMENTS.md\nbun.lock\nbunfig.toml\neslint.config.js\nexamples/basic-usage.mjs\nexperiments/reproduce-npm-launcher.mjs\nexperiments/test-regex-pattern.mjs\ngh-load-issue.mjs\npackage-lock.json\npackage.json\nscripts/changeset-version.mjs\nscripts/check-file-size.mjs\nscripts/create-github-release.mjs\nscripts/create-manual-changeset.mjs\nscripts/format-github-release.mjs\nscripts/format-release-notes.mjs\nscripts/instant-version-bump.mjs\nscripts/package-smoke-test.mjs\nscripts/publis